**What landed:**
- `src/lib/server/generation.ts` — dropped the `ralph` stage entirely. After init_course, parse `course.json` with `CourseSchema`, flatten `modules.flatMap(m => m.lessons)`, then for each lesson spawn ONE `claude -p '<natural-language brief naming generate_lesson + both slugs>' --dangerously-skip-permissions` in the main repo CWD. Read the produced `courses/<slug>/lessons/<lesson-slug>.json` and validate with `LessonSchema`. Failures (non-zero exit, missing file, schema mismatch) get recorded in `failedLessons` and the loop continues. New exports: `defaultLessonCommand`, `FailedLesson`. `SpawnDeps.ralphCommand` removed in favour of `lessonCommand`. The `done` event now carries `failedLessons: FailedLesson[]`; `error` may carry it too. If every lesson fails, finalize as `error`. Per-lesson `progress` events emit explicitly; the old `tryParseProgress` log-line scraper is gone.
- `src/lib/server/generation.test.ts` — added 7 new cases (multi-lesson happy path, lessonCommand factory injection, single-lesson failure isolation, post-spawn LessonSchema validation, cancel mid-run, defaultLessonCommand prompt + slug safety) and updated 2 existing cases to write a stub `course.json` + lesson before letting children exit. All ralph-spawn assertions removed.
- `scripts/ralph/{prd.json, progress.txt}` — flipped US-097 `passes: true`; appended progress entry with learnings.

